[#:seon.task{:name "one-weighted-cache-under-a-memory-cap"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "About fifteen defonce caches each carry a code-constant entry bound and no byte cap (seon.db arity-commit 92.6 MB, projection 12.8 MB, arity-base 9.0 MB; seon.sci.eval base-context 27.4 MB, program-identity, refusal-recording; seon.test.runner reach-holders 16.7 MB; the build-projection memos). Owner rulings: every cache configurable, a library not a hand-rolled cache, one fixed memory cap. Recommended: one Caffeine cache keyed [cache-id key] with maximumWeight from one byte dial and a weigher recorded at insert (~60 lines, roughly net neutral)."
             :must-read #{seon.db/carried-projection seon.sci.eval/base-ctx seon.test.runner/reach-memberships}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/mem-idle-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/perf-profile-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "cache-weights-run-three-times-the-retained-bytes"
             :kind :function
             :intent "seon.cache weights run about 3x high: 156 MB really retained against 498 MB of estimated weight; the two test-runner reach kinds account for 340 MB of the weight (heap-live lane, MAT, default, 2026-10-08). The byte budget therefore does not measure bytes and evicts too early. Fix the weighers (shared structure is weighed once per kind that holds it) so weight tracks retained bytes. Done when for the reach kinds the summed weight is within 1.5x of the measured retained size."
             :must-read #{seon.cache/create seon.test.runner/reach-entries}}]
